# DURABLE REPRO — the `&`-in-an-OWNING-POSITION class, costume 5 of 7:
# an ARRAY-LITERAL ELEMENT (`[&c.fd]`).
#
# ⚠ THIS COSTUME IS NOT "the sigil is ignored" — IT IS A GARBAGE-VALUE
# MISCOMPILE.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg): `gg check` is clean and both backends
# accept, then store a RAW STACK ADDRESS into an `int` slot:
#     C    -> 281474930661984
#     LLVM -> 281474478852760
# (the exact digits are ASLR-dependent; what is stable is that the value is a
# pointer, not 10). `ggdef` REJECTS ("`&`-alias into an owning position is not
# valid").
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check`. An array-literal element position is an
# ownership boundary — the array must own its elements — so there is nothing to
# write through to, and D31 full-strict gives `&` no other meaning.
#
# The `fd` seed is COMPUTED, not a literal, so the address cannot be
# const-folded into a plausible-looking constant.
#
# The DROP facet of this same costume has its own fixture:
# `security/sound_amp_array_literal_duplicate_drop.gg` (a bare-param root plus a
# user `Drop` runs the drop TWICE on both backends).
#
# See `sound_amp_owning_position_ctor.gg` for the full sibling list and the
# ruling this class rests on.
struct Counter:
    int fd

int seed():
    return 10

void main():
    Counter c = Counter(seed())
    Vector[int] arr = [&c.fd]
    print(arr[0])
